 "notes": [
  "no_pssm positives are real Acrs with the PSSM block zeroed -- the identical input transformation the pipeline sees when PSI-BLAST returns no hits. Only 1 of 64 Acrs natively lacks a PSSM, so ablation is the only way to get positives in this regime.",
  "Synthetic negatives are RETAINED, but scored only within no_pssm where their ~0.999 is unremarkable rather than Acr-like.",
  "AcrNET is not uninformative without a PSSM (AUROC 0.7906 vs ablated phage, 0.8135 vs synthetic); the signal sits in the extreme tail, hence the finer no_pssm bounds.",
  "Superseded acrnet_scores.csv (AUROC 0.8831) was irreproducible: neither per-protein nor chunked scoring regenerates it from these features (max delta 0.9988). Discarded."
 ]
